      "comment": "First a leather corselet, then any cuirass, even one of linen (Suet. Galb. 19; Lewis &amp; Short); also a breastwork on a rampart (Caes. BG 5.39). De Vaan lists it among the derivatives of <span lang=\"la\">lōrum</span>, a thong, while reporting that some take it for a loan word."
